cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "ICU vital-sign record density: source-stream and site-level variation"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a retrospective data-quality study of vital-sign record
  density across MIMIC-IV and eICU-CRD, decomposing variance by data stream,
  database, contributing site and care unit. Version 1.1.0 added a
  plausibility-restricted primary cohort, a threshold sweep across observation
  floors, a fitted negative-binomial generalized linear mixed model for the
  count outcome, duplicate-timestamp and covariate-missingness checks,
  excluded-stay characterisation, and entry-order sensitivity. Version 1.1.1
  added the hospital-attribute conditioning analysis. Version 1.1.2 adds
  bias-corrected and accelerated bootstrap intervals for every Gaussian
  variance partition coefficient, from a closed-form evaluation of the
  restricted maximum likelihood objective validated against statsmodels
  MixedLM; negative-binomial and zero-truncated negative-binomial mixed models
  with a hurdle specification for gaps exceeding 2 hours, their
  profile-likelihood intervals and their observed-scale equivalents in closed
  form; and a 10,000-permutation hospital-attribute null using the plus-one
  estimator, corrected across all ten tests. Version 1.1.3 refits the
  Poisson comparison with the count-model routine, so that the Poisson and
  negative binomial coefficients reported together come from one estimator,
  and adds the correlation between record count and the count of intervals
  exceeding 30 minutes. Version 1.1.4 adds the availability of the eICU-CRD
  APACHE physiology table on every analysis set, deposited as a negative
  result. Version 1.1.5 deposits the scripts, outputs and console logs behind
  the dispersion statistics and denominators supplied at copyediting, and
  changes no earlier script or output. The published article cites version
  1.1.4. The DOI above is the concept DOI and resolves to the most recent
  version.
